From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: About's eMMC value translated

The previous patch's eMMC row built its value in English inside
kiln_hardware, so a Russian screen showed "(maker 0xEC)" in English.
kiln_hardware now only reads: read_emmc() returns the name, maker ID,
PRV and size in sectors. The About panel reads it once and turns it
into text in populate_info_rows() with lv_tr() and the English format
strings as keys, so the system module needs no LVGL and the row
follows the language each time About opens. The name and "PRV" stay
untranslated. The keys are in en.yml and, with Russian values, in
ru.yml; other languages show English.

Also an eMMC size of 0 sectors is left out instead of "0.0 GiB".

The tests check the fields, and an eMMC without a name, maker or size.
---
 include/system/kiln_hardware.h        | 23 +++++++++++++---
 include/ui_settings_about.h           |  6 +++++
 src/system/kiln_hardware.cpp          | 36 ++++++++++++-------------
 src/ui/settings/ui_settings_about.cpp | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 tests/unit/test_kiln_hardware.cpp     | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
 translations/en.yml                   |  2 ++
 translations/ru.yml                   |  2 ++
 7 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/system/kiln_hardware.h b/include/system/kiln_hardware.h
index 8f2a254bf2..5e7d369308 100644
--- a/include/system/kiln_hardware.h
+++ b/include/system/kiln_hardware.h
@@ -9,16 +9,31 @@
  * (58A398, A31M8C, MMC8GB so far). The About panel shows it.
  */
 
+#include <optional>
 #include <string>
 
 namespace helix::kiln_hardware {
 
+/// What the eMMC row shows
+struct EmmcInfo {
+    std::string name;               ///< the CID's product name ("A31M8C")
+    std::optional<unsigned> maker;  ///< the CID's manufacturer ID (0xEC)
+    std::string prv;                ///< the product revision as sysfs gives it ("0x30"); "" none
+    unsigned long long sectors = 0; ///< 512-byte sectors; 0 unknown
+
+    /// The size in GiB; nullopt when the size is unknown or 0
+    std::optional<double> size_gib() const;
+};
+
 /**
- * @brief The eMMC row: "A31M8C (maker 0xEC), PRV 0x30, 58.2 GiB".
+ * @brief The eMMC row's fields, from /sys/block/mmcblk0.
  *
- * From /sys/block/mmcblk0; "" when there is no eMMC there. @p root is the
- * test seam: the files are read below it.
+ * nullopt when there is no eMMC there (no device, an SD card, no name).
+ * This module only reads; the About panel turns the fields into the
+ * translated row text ("A31M8C (maker 0xEC), PRV 0x30, 58.2 GiB"), so
+ * nothing here depends on LVGL. @p root is the test seam: the files are
+ * read below it.
  */
-std::string emmc_summary(const std::string& root = "");
+std::optional<EmmcInfo> read_emmc(const std::string& root = "");
 
 } // namespace helix::kiln_hardware
diff --git a/include/ui_settings_about.h b/include/ui_settings_about.h
